## 16. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA / DEFINITION OF DONE
The MVP is done only when ALL of the following are verified (write Playwright/Vitest tests where practical and a manual QA checklist in `/docs/QA.md`):
1. A new user can sign up, verify email, create a workspace, and land in the onboarding wizard.
2. A user can connect Google Sheets and Airtable via OAuth, map fields with auto-suggestions, run a dry-run, activate, and see records appear in the destination, all within 10 minutes.
3. Notion and HubSpot each work as both source and destination for at least one object type (Notion database; HubSpot Contacts).
4. CSV upload works as a source and as a destination (export), with type detection.
5. Two-way sync works for at least Sheets ↔ Airtable, and all four conflict rules behave as specified (tests prove each). Manual review items appear in the Review Queue and resolve correctly.
6. No infinite sync loops: after a two-way sync stabilizes, a subsequent run produces zero writes (test).
7. Re-running the same job or retrying after a simulated crash creates no duplicate records (idempotency test).
8. Rate-limit (429) and 5xx responses trigger backoff and eventual success; permanent failures land in the dead-letter queue and can be replayed from the UI.
9. Expired/revoked OAuth tokens mark the connection "needs reconnect", pause dependent syncs, and notify the owner.
